{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And in all the land of your possession.</b> To include houses and a Hebrew slave — and this matter is spelled out in Kiddushin, first chapter (21a). According to its plain sense, it is joined to the passage after it: that one who sells his possession may redeem it after two years — either he or his relative — and the buyer cannot prevent it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:20.440897591Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}